Commit:     Mark Shank <mark.shank@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 21 15:50:18 2026 -0400

    Speed up the V4.1 decode top-512
    
    V4.1 decode picks the 512 best index scores for each token. For that case (V4 Flash is unchanged), each block is sorted with SIMD shuffles, each merge of two sorted runs keeps only the best 512, the 512 winners of the radix select are sorted together in one pass, and when scoring is limited to candidate blocks, the candidate list is built once per token. The selected indices and their order are the same as before on any input without NaNs. This builds on Tarjei Mandt's radix select and candidate-block scoring (af7c02b5, 2d5ef0d3).
    
    DS4_METAL_DISABLE_V41_DECODE_TOPK=1 uses the previous kernels.

